Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: the corner where a knife edge runs on along its line into an
edge whose faces meet at an angle is refused in words (mitcad#1988).

A bite cut part of the way along a wall (a block with a cylinder of the
block's half width cut from below into its front, tangent to the side
wall): along the line where the wall meets the bite's cylinder
tangentially (a knife edge, the wedge between them of 0 degrees) and,
past the bite's end plane, the front face square, the two edges are one
tangent chain. The ball of a rounding lies two radii into the wedge along
the knife edge (sqrt(260 r) from the front for the bite of 65) and in the
corner along the square edge: it jumps at their common vertex. OCCT ends
the contours there, each a stripe of its own, and the vertex, with four
edges and two stripes, went to PerformMoreThreeCorner, whose plate gave a
valid body of the wrong shape (a surface far from the edges, more volume
than the block). The body asked for has the end plane grown under the
knife's tip up to the square edge's rounding and a new edge along the wall
between the two contacts, which no corner of the fillet builds.

- ChFi3d_Builder::RefuseKnifeEndsOnLine, from PerformFilletOnVertex for
  two stripes at a vertex of more than three edges, before
  PerformMoreThreeCorner: where each stripe has one end there, their edges
  go on along one line (within the angular tolerance), one is a knife edge
  and the other not, and they have one face in common, it throws
  Standard_Failure "a knife edge running on along its line into an edge
  whose faces meet at an angle: the ball jumps at the vertex between
  them". The corner fails at that vertex as any corner does (the
  vertex is faulty, FailedCornerMessage says why): the failure is
  reported, never a body built from it. Elsewhere it returns, nothing
  changed.
- ChFi3d_IsKnifeEdge (ChFi3d_Builder_0): the faces' normals, sampled along
  the edge with the faces' orientations, all within a thousandth of a
  radian of opposite.
- No catch is added.

Each such edge alone still rounds: the knife edge's stripe ends on the
end plane, which grows over the tip's section (1770's start). MitCad rounds
the knife edges first and the other edges on that result
(knife_line_apart in geometry/src/dressup.cpp).

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_knife_chain.cpp: the block with the bite,
the knife edge and the square edge on its line in one fillet with 1 and 3:
not done, the corner failed at the vertex on the bite's end plane with the
message above (before the patch: done, a valid body 6611 mm3 larger than
the expected one at 1); the knife edge alone valid with the exact volume;
MitCad's fillet of the chain valid with the exact volume.

